1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,825
Chapter-14. 
Ethan Bruce POV

2
00:00:02,825 --> 00:00:04,503
A week of silence passed.

3
00:00:04,503 --> 00:00:06,457
Seven days of dead air.

4
00:00:06,457 --> 00:00:09,280
The city wasn't just quiet; it was holding its breath.

5
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:13,086
The rumors had already begun to rot the foundation of our reputation.

6
00:00:13,086 --> 00:00:16,559
The other families were whispering in the dark corners of their clubs.

7
00:00:16,559 --> 00:00:18,316
The Underboss lost his wife.

8
00:00:18,316 --> 00:00:20,618
The Bruce family is bleeding.They are weak.

9
00:00:20,618 --> 00:00:22,475
I didn't give a damn about the rumors.

10
00:00:22,475 --> 00:00:26,294
The only thing that mattered was the silence on the other end of the phone.

11
00:00:26,294 --> 00:00:27,801
I needed to break something.

12
00:00:27,801 --> 00:00:30,350
I drove to the penthouse.Ilene's apartment.

13
00:00:30,350 --> 00:00:32,092
The golden cage I paid for.

14
00:00:32,092 --> 00:00:35,283
The place I visited to pay my debts in flesh and guilt.

15
00:00:35,283 --> 00:00:37,570
I hadn't spoken to her since the hospital.

16
00:00:37,570 --> 00:00:43,234
I had sent doctors, nurses, and a rotation of guards, but I hadn't stepped foot inside myself.

17
00:00:43,234 --> 00:00:49,134
I couldn't look at her without seeing Aurora falling out of that van, like a broken doll discarded on the pavement.

18
00:00:49,134 --> 00:00:50,991
But tonight, I needed noise.

19
00:00:50,991 --> 00:00:53,412
I needed to scream at someone who deserved it.

20
00:00:53,412 --> 00:00:56,752
I didn't buzz up.I bypassed the doorman with the master key.

21
00:00:56,752 --> 00:01:01,484
I took the private elevator to the top floor, watching the numbers climb like a countdown.

22
00:01:01,484 --> 00:01:02,895
The doors slid open.

23
00:01:02,895 --> 00:01:08,728
I heard music.Jazz.Smooth, expensive, and utterly discordant with the chaos in my mind.

24
00:01:08,728 --> 00:01:09,606
And laughter.

25
00:01:09,606 --> 00:01:14,536
Ilene's laugh.It wasn't the hysterical, gasping sob she used to manipulate me.

26
00:01:14,536 --> 00:01:17,722
It was a throat-deep, satisfied sound of victory.

27
00:01:17,722 --> 00:01:19,669
"He's a wreck, Leo.It's pathetic."

28
00:01:19,669 --> 00:01:20,446
I froze.

29
00:01:20,446 --> 00:01:20,994
Leo.

30
00:01:20,994 --> 00:01:23,704
Leo Vance.The Capo of the rival syndicate.

31
00:01:23,704 --> 00:01:27,453
The man whose soldiers had tried to run my trucks off the road last month.

32
00:01:27,453 --> 00:01:32,695
"He's running around the city like a headless chicken," a male voice drawled, dripping with amusement.

33
00:01:32,695 --> 00:01:35,364
"My guys said he looks like he hasn't slept in a week."

34
00:01:35,364 --> 00:01:39,419
"Good," Ilene said.I heard the distinct clink of crystal."He deserves it.

35
00:01:39,419 --> 00:01:42,130
Treating me like a dirty secret for five years.

36
00:01:42,130 --> 00:01:45,819
Now that the bitch is gone, he'll come crawling back.He always does."

37
00:01:45,819 --> 00:01:50,289
My hand didn't just hover over my gun; it itched to empty the magazine.

38
00:01:50,289 --> 00:01:52,103
"You're sure she's gone?"Leo asked.

39
00:01:52,103 --> 00:01:54,954
"Oh, she's gone.The kidnapping scared her straight.

40
00:01:54,954 --> 00:01:56,249
I told you it would work."

41
00:01:56,249 --> 00:01:59,708
The world didn't just tilt; the ground vanished beneath my feet.

42
00:01:59,708 --> 00:02:01,291
I stepped out of the elevator.

43
00:02:01,291 --> 00:02:04,139
They were in the living room, a tableau of betrayal.

44
00:02:04,139 --> 00:02:08,666
Leo Vance was lounging on my leather sofa, his boots resting on my coffee table.

45
00:02:08,666 --> 00:02:14,246
Ilene was straddling his lap, a glass of wine in her hand, celebrating the destruction of my life.

46
00:02:14,246 --> 00:02:15,768
They froze when they saw me.

47
00:02:15,768 --> 00:02:17,183
Ilene dropped the glass.

48
00:02:17,183 --> 00:02:22,594
It shattered on the floor, red wine splashing across the hardwood like a fresh arterial spray.

49
00:02:22,594 --> 00:02:23,881
"Ethan," she breathed.

50
00:02:23,881 --> 00:02:25,275
Her face went ashen.

51
00:02:25,275 --> 00:02:26,684
Leo went for his gun.

52
00:02:26,684 --> 00:02:27,620
He was fast.

53
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:28,662
But I was possessed.

54
00:02:28,662 --> 00:02:30,090
I didn't draw my weapon.

55
00:02:30,090 --> 00:02:32,790
I crossed the room in two predatory strides.

56
00:02:32,790 --> 00:02:39,465
I snatched the heavy wine bottle from the table and swung it in a violent arc, smashing it directly across Leo's face.

57
00:02:39,465 --> 00:02:40,279
He screamed.

58
00:02:40,279 --> 00:02:42,752
The sound was music-a symphony of pain.

59
00:02:42,752 --> 00:02:47,576
He fell back onto the sofa, blood pouring from his nose and forehead, blinding him.

60
00:02:47,576 --> 00:02:52,781
Ilene scrambled off him, backing away until she hit the wall, her hands raised in surrender.

61
00:02:52,781 --> 00:02:54,982
"Ethan, wait!I can explain!"

62
00:02:54,982 --> 00:02:55,941
I ignored her.

63
00:02:55,941 --> 00:02:58,343
I grabbed Leo by the throat and hauled him up.

64
00:02:58,343 --> 00:03:01,915
He was a big man, but fear makes even the heaviest men light.

65
00:03:01,915 --> 00:03:04,582
"The kidnapping," I said.My voice was calm.

66
00:03:04,582 --> 00:03:07,046
Terrifyingly, unnaturally calm.

67
00:03:07,046 --> 00:03:09,573
"She paid me!She bankrolled the whole thing!

68
00:03:09,573 --> 00:03:11,606
She said you wouldn't pick up the phone!"

69
00:03:11,606 --> 00:03:15,344
I tightened my grip, feeling his windpipe strain against my fingers.

70
00:03:15,344 --> 00:03:16,733
"And the van?" I asked.

71
00:03:16,733 --> 00:03:17,907
"The men who took her?"

72
00:03:17,907 --> 00:03:20,538
"My guys," Leo wheezed, his eyes bulging.

73
00:03:20,538 --> 00:03:21,832
"Just a scare tactic.

74
00:03:21,832 --> 00:03:23,224
We weren't gonna kill her.

75
00:03:23,224 --> 00:03:25,353
Just... rough her up.Make you look bad."

76
00:03:25,353 --> 00:03:26,443
I looked at Ilene.

77
00:03:26,443 --> 00:03:29,216
She was trembling against the wall, a portrait of guilt.

78
00:03:29,216 --> 00:03:30,629
"You set it up," I said.

79
00:03:30,629 --> 00:03:33,606
"I did it for us!" she screamed, her voice cracking.

80
00:03:33,606 --> 00:03:35,253
"She was in the way, Ethan!

81
00:03:35,253 --> 00:03:37,146
She was poisoning you against me!"

82
00:03:37,146 --> 00:03:40,448
"She called me," I said, the memory cutting through me like a knife.

83
00:03:40,448 --> 00:03:41,820
"When she was in that van.

84
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:43,564
She called me on the red line."

85
00:03:43,564 --> 00:03:45,793
Ilene's eyes widened in horror.

86
00:03:45,793 --> 00:03:47,529
"And I declined it," I whispered.

87
00:03:47,529 --> 00:03:49,335
"Because you were holding my hand."

88
00:03:49,335 --> 00:03:54,121
The rage that exploded in my chest wasn't hot.It was cold.Absolute zero.

89
00:03:54,121 --> 00:03:59,939
I had let my wife be dragged off the street by my enemy because I was busy comforting the woman who paid him to do it.

90
00:03:59,939 --> 00:04:01,274
I looked back at Leo.

91
00:04:01,274 --> 00:04:02,701
"You touched her," I said.

92
00:04:02,701 --> 00:04:05,671
"I didn't," Leo choked out, clawing at my wrist.

93
00:04:05,671 --> 00:04:07,670
"My guys... they just grabbed her."

94
00:04:07,670 --> 00:04:09,250
"Someone twisted her arm.

95
00:04:09,250 --> 00:04:10,634
Someone broke her ribs."

96
00:04:10,634 --> 00:04:11,778
"Ethan, please-"

97
00:04:11,778 --> 00:04:15,191
I threw him onto the floor with enough force to crack the floorboards.

98
00:04:15,191 --> 00:04:16,999
"You broke my property," I said.

99
00:04:16,999 --> 00:04:21,002
I unbuttoned my cuffs, rolling up my sleeves with methodical precision.

100
00:04:21,002 --> 00:04:22,088
"Now I break you."
